Store each tab's space id and carry it through session restore.

SpaceTabHelper holds the id of the space a tab belongs to; none means the
default space. The id is written as tab extra data when it changes, and on
restore it is read back like Chromium's own extra data.

Chromium writes tab extra data only when it changes, and drops it whenever
SessionServiceBase::BuildCommandsForTab() writes a tab from scratch: when the
session file is rewritten, and when session restore records a restored tab.
Without a hook there, a tab's space survives one restart and is lost on the
next. Closed tabs keep their space through
BrowserLiveTabContext::GetExtraDataForTab().

